  "|The Clifford Constitution of 1922 was significant because it:|Granted Nigeria independence|Introduced elective representation in Nigeria for the first time|Created the First Republic|Divided Nigeria into North and South": "colonial",
  "|Which theory holds that the state originated through force and conquest?|Social contract theory|Force or conquest theory|Divine right theory|Evolutionary theory": "concepts",
  "|The concept of 'balance of power' in international relations refers to:|Equal distribution of economic resources|A system where no single state becomes dominant by ensuring roughly equal power among major states|Equal military spending|UN peacekeeping operations": "foreign-policy",
  "|Local government exists at which tier in Nigeria?|First tier|Second tier|Third tier|Fourth tier": "local-government",
  "|The concept of 'rule of law' as developed by A.V. Dicey includes all of the following EXCEPT:|Supremacy of law over arbitrary power|Equality before the law|The constitution is the result of rights of individuals as defined by courts|Laws are made only by the military": "constitution",
